# Windmill Lane - BONANZA's course 3 (SPEC.md 128.12.9): the course wave 3's
# obstacles are judged on, built for the RUBBER ball.  Everything wave 3 adds
# is on it:
#  - two WINDMILLS, each a KEEP tunnel through one house to a tier beside it,
#    entered along -y through a doorway on the house face with its rotor
#    standing on it.  The route passes the right one (an explicit seed, 16, so
#    the autopilot's first approach finds the gate open, SPEC.md 128.12.15
#    item 4); the left one keeps its derived seed (36);
#  - three BUMPERS, a cluster on a green walled with bumper rails: the route
#    crosses it and ricochets off two posts;
#  - a DROP chute down from the green onto F, the finishing tier, 3 units below
#    its mouth (rubber bounces, steel is stunned, glass shatters: the tool
#    prints it);
#  - a LAUNCH cannon from F over a gap onto G, the goal ledge.  Its flight runs
#    along a cell row (constant s) from a lone mouth tile to G's front corner,
#    with nothing in front of it, so it and the chute's fall cross no OCC cell
#    (the layout 128.11.13 item 8 asked of TRIAL's flights); a wall at the end
#    of the row and a lower terrace in front of G keep a bounce off the corner
#    on the course;
#  - a LIFT (L 6, P 256, the default dwell: v 192) in a shaft on F's east
#    edge, between F (its high dock, 2 units) and a low island 6 units
#    below it (-4), beside the route and in no window a windmill shares: a
#    ball rolled off F into the shaft lands on the slab wherever it is.
# F is sand, so the chute's bounces die on it before the cannon's drain.
course MILL "Windmill Lane"
width 64
ball rubber

# A, the start tier, and the windmills' house behind it
floor rect  6  9 11 14  flat 16
wall  rect  6  5 12  9  flat 22
# B, east of the house, 4 units up; C west of it
floor rect 12  5 16  9  flat 20
floor rect  3  5  6  9  flat 18
# B's descent along +y to the green
floor rect 14  9 16 17  ramp y 9 17 20 8
# the green, walled with bumper rails
floor rect 12 17 18 22  flat 8
wall  rect 12 16 14 17  flat 10
wall  rect 16 16 18 17  flat 10
wall  rect 11 17 12 22  flat 9
wall  rect 18 17 19 22  flat 9
wall  rect 12 22 19 23  flat 9
surface bounce rect 11 17 12 22
surface bounce rect 18 17 19 22
surface bounce rect 12 22 19 23
# the chute's last wall, F the finishing tier, the cannon's body and its mouth
wall  tile 19 20        flat 9
floor rect 20 15 26 23  flat 2
surface sand rect 20 15 26 23
wall  tile 23 23        flat 2.5
floor tile 23 24        flat 2
# the lift's low rim, an island in front of its shaft
floor rect 27 18 29 20  flat -4
# G, the goal ledge, over the gap
floor rect 18 24 22 27  flat 1
floor rect 18 27 22 28  flat 0.5
wall  rect 18 28 22 29  flat 1
wall  rect 17 24 18 27  flat 1.5
goal  rect 18 24 20 26  flat 1

tube keep   9 9  12 6  via 9 6
prop windmill 9 9  seed 16
tube keep   7 9   5 7  via 7 7
prop windmill 7 9
prop bumper 14 19
prop bumper 16 18
prop bumper 16 20
tube drop  17 20  20 20  out +x  height 3
tube launch 23 22  23 24  speed -192 192 480
prop platform 26 18 6

start 9 12

# The autopilot's route (the benchmark's MILL leg, SPEC.md 128.12.9): into the
# windmill, over the green, down the chute, through the cannon to the goal - no
# fall in 1,289 steps (`bbcourse.py --selfcheck` item 8).
way  9 12
way  9  9
way 12  6
way 14  7
way 14 13
way 14 18
way 17 20
way 20 20
way 23 20
way 23 22
way 23 24
way 19 25
